SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] 11/16/2026: Androscoggin County Courthouse to
  Undergo Remediation Efforts
DESCRIPTION:Home\nSkip to top navigation\nSkip to side navigation\nSkip to
  content\nSkip to footer\nCOURT ALERTS IN EFFECT.\nSee Active Alerts\nHome
 \n→\nNews & Announcements\nAndroscoggin County Courthouse to Undergo Rem
 ediation Efforts\nDate:\n11/16/2026\nEnvironmental testing conducted after
  concerns were raised about the condition of the Androscoggin County Court
 house has revealed elevated levels of mold in some areas of the building. 
 The Judicial Branch ceased operations in all affected areas of the buildin
 g.  The Judicial Branch is working with Androscoggin County\, who owns the
  building\, to remove the mold and make needed repairs.  The building will
  be retested to make sure that the problems are eradicated before reopenin
 g any parts of the building with elevated mold levels.\nSupporting documen
 ts\nPress Release (PDF)\nhttps://www.courts.maine.gov/news/article.html?id
 =13368575
URL:https://www.courts.maine.gov/news/article.html?id=13368575
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
