SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Magnuson-Stevens Fishery Conservation and Man
 agement Act Provisions\; Fisheries of the Northeastern United States\; Fra
 mework Adjustment 7 to the Atlantic Spiny Dogfish Fishery Management Plan
DESCRIPTION:NMFS proposes measures included in Framework Adjustment 7 to t
 he Spiny Dogfish Fishery Management Plan (FMP)\, as recommended by the Mid
 -Atlantic and New England Fishery Management Councils. Framework 7 propose
 s fishing year 2026 and projected 2027 specifications\, which would establ
 ish allowable harvest levels for the spiny dogfish fishery to prevent over
 fishing while enabling optimum yield based on the best scientific informat
 ion available. Framework 7 also proposes changes to the Atlantic spiny dog
 fish accountability measures intended to provide the commercial fishery wi
 th greater flexibility by no longer requiring full payback of annual catch
  limit (ACL) overages when the Atlantic spiny dogfish stock is considered 
 healthy.\nhttps://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/10/13/2026-20863/
 magnuson-stevens-fishery-conservation-and-management-act-provisions-fisher
 ies-of-the-northeastern
URL:https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/10/13/2026-20863/magnus
 on-stevens-fishery-conservation-and-management-act-provisions-fisheries-of
 -the-northeastern
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:e2b16b075b89405c@role-environmental-land-use.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20261010T122726Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261013
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Fisheries of the Northeastern United States\;
  Summer Flounder Fishery\; 2026 Commercial Quota Harvested for the State o
 f Maine
DESCRIPTION:NMFS announces that the 2026 summer flounder commercial quota 
 allocated to the State of Maine has been harvested. Vessels issued a comme
 rcial Federal fisheries permit for the summer flounder fishery may not lan
 d summer flounder in Maine for the remainder of calendar year 2026\, unles
 s additional quota becomes available through a transfer from another state
 . Regulations governing the summer flounder fishery require publication of
  this notification to advise Maine that the quota has been harvested\, and
  to advise vessel permit holders and dealer permit holders that no Federal
  commercial quota is available for landing summer flounder in Maine.\nhttp
 s://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/10/13/2026-20861/fisheries-of-t
